# Cloudflare Workers static-asset redirects. Parsed by Workers out of the
# deployed asset directory (Vite copies public/ into dist/, the same way it
# carries _headers), evaluated top-down, first match wins.
#
# This file carries NO rules, and `hosting.test.ts` keeps it that way. What
# follows is why, so that nobody adds them back.
#
# Phase 6 Task 1 (#65, P6.1). T-02 fixes the candidate URL at
# /<workspace-slug>/<test-slug>, a path with no file behind it, and tried to
# serve it from here.

# WITHDRAWN 2026-10-20, live on the deployed Worker:
#
#   /assets/*  /assets/:splat  200
#   /fonts/*   /fonts/:splat   200
#   /:workspaceSlug/:testSlug  /exam.html  200
#
# The pass-throughs do not take effect — a 200 rewrite to its own path reads
# as a loop and is dropped — so EVERY two-segment path fell through to the
# fallback, including /assets/<hashed>.css and /assets/<hashed>.js. Measured
# on the deployed Worker: an asset that exists in dist/ answered 307 to /exam,
# and so did /assets/definitely-not-here.css, which should have been a 404.
# The landing page lost all styling and /admin loaded no script at all.
#
# The fallback also failed at its own job: /<ws>/<test> answered 307 to /exam
# rather than rewriting, because html_handling turns a rewrite to /exam.html
# into a redirect that drops the .html — and the slug pair with it, which
# src/exam-main.tsx needs to know which test to load.
#
# No test caught this: the suite asserts this file's CONTENT, and nothing
# exercises Cloudflare's asset router, which only exists in production.
#
# The candidate URL needs the Worker, not this file. `apps/api/src/index.ts`
# serves it now: a two-segment path is answered with the exam shell fetched
# from the ASSETS binding under the original URL, which is a rewrite the
# asset router cannot be asked to perform. Nothing goes back in here.
